// Title: A Rule Has Been Deleted From The Windows Firewall Exception List
// ID: c187c075-bb3e-4c62-b4fa-beae0ffc211f
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-02-19
// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1686.003
// Description: Detects when a single rules or all of the rules have been deleted from the Windows Defender Firewall
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

any where (((winlog.event_id == 2006 or winlog.event_id == 2052)) and not (((ModifyingApplication == "") or ((ModifyingApplication startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\" or ModifyingApplication startswith "C:\\Program Files\\" or ModifyingApplication startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\")) or (ModifyingApplication == null) or (ModifyingApplication == "C:\\Windows\\System32\\svchost.exe"))) and not ((ModifyingApplication startswith "C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Platform\\" and ModifyingApplication endswith "\\MsMpEng.exe")))
